Windows: upstream gives `-DUSE_SETMODE` to cjpeg/djpeg/jpegtran only, so the
`setmode(fileno(std…), O_BINARY)` calls rdjpgcom and wrjpgcom already carry
are compiled out. wrjpgcom writes its JPEG to stdout only, so every file it
produced had each 0x0A expanded to 0x0D 0x0A (a corrupt JPEG, always), and
rdjpgcom failed on stdin ("Premature EOF in JPEG file").

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -876,6 +876,8 @@
   add_executable(rdjpgcom src/rdjpgcom.c)
 
   add_executable(wrjpgcom src/wrjpgcom.c)
+  target_compile_definitions(rdjpgcom PRIVATE USE_SETMODE)
+  target_compile_definitions(wrjpgcom PRIVATE USE_SETMODE)
 endif()
 
 
